Q2: max min-clear-q found across all restarts (the empirical window ceiling for DC):
  random high-Vmax: max min-clear-q = 26
  => if the ceiling keeps rising with Vmax, the window is UNBOUNDED (Route B is not a fixed finite check);
     if it saturates, there is a bounded window. (Structural: blocking q needs a multiple => diameter >= q.)
